  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-iframe-element\n\n> When an iframe element is removed from a document, the user agent must discard the nested browsing context, if any.\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#a-browsing-context-is-discarded\n\n> Other browsing contexts must be discarded once their WindowProxy object is eligible for garbage collection.\n\nIt's not clear for me what should happen if\na) there exists a reference to the WindowProxy of the iframe's nested browsing context, and\nb) the iframe element is removed from a document.\n\n```\n// Save a reference to the WindowProxy.\nvar windowProxy = iframe.contentWindow;\n// Remove the iframe element from a document.\niframe.remove();\n```\n\nIn this case, the nested browsing context of the iframe element should be discarded or not?\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-iframe-element seems saying that the user agent must discard the browsing context.\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#a-browsing-context-is-discarded seems saying that the browsing context must not be discarded because the WindowProxy is not eligible for garbage collection.\n",
